{
  "experiment": "E-E",
  "data_classes": [
    "SIM-sremu",
    "ANALYTIC",
    "MEAS"
  ],
  "description": "Stock GNU Radio 3.10 DQPSK modem (gr-zeromq REQ/REP, gr-digital) through sremu's raw REQ/REP mode: link quality vs RIS configuration, in-run switch timing, bitwise reproducibility, lockstep real-time factor",
  "assumptions": [
    "SIM geometry gr_ris_ber.yaml: ideal 1-bit 16 x 16 RIS at 3.5 GHz, TX/RX 5 m at -30/+20 deg, direct path behind a 40 dB partition, 1 MS/s, NF 7 dB",
    "BLER = fraction of consecutive uncoded 100-symbol (200-bit) windows of GNU Radio's decision stream with an error (no coding, no CRC)",
    "SNR estimated from the received IQ against the regenerated TX IQ (LS fit)",
    "array-factor prediction: isotropic point cells, no cell pattern or obliquity (internal consistency check, not a measurement)",
    "lockstep: virtual time follows the sample exchange; the real-time factor is virtual seconds per wall second on the stated host (MEAS)",
    "GNU Radio decisions of the first 20 ms (30 ms after a switch) are not scored"
  ],
